# The cartridge itself -- copyrighted, not distributed. Supply your own
# legally-owned dump named exactly as below (or edit the .command scripts)
# to reproduce anything in this repo.
*.a78

# Generated disassembly -- fully reproducible from annotations.json + the
# ROM via the a7800-toolkit (see README.md). Not committed: this literally
# is the copyrighted machine code in readable form, plus it's stale the
# moment annotations.json changes.
/src/
/build/

# Audio/video captures and renders -- derived from the cartridge's own
# copyrighted graphics, and reproducible from the .inp recordings plus the
# toolkit's capture tools.
*.wav
*.trk
*.log
/snap/

# Raw memory dumps -- contain copyrighted ROM/RAM bytes, reproducible from
# a recording + a probe script (see docs/FINDINGS.md for which probe made
# each one).
*.bin

# Local MAME config -- machine-specific, regenerated on first run.
/cfg/

# Derived analysis manifests -- reproducible from the ROM + recordings via
# the tools/*.lua scripts. Not the primary record (annotations.json and
# docs/FINDINGS.md are); regenerate as needed.
*-out.json

.DS_Store

# AppleDouble sidecars. macOS writes a `._name` beside every file when it
# copies to a filesystem that cannot hold a resource fork -- a FAT or NTFS
# volume, a USB stick, an SMB share. They are metadata, never content, and
# copying this repository through one produces dozens of them.
._*
